IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cat-owner`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"); a question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The Act puts its duties on three kinds of person who would ask it questions:
--   - the owner, or the person who keeps the cat: the baseline's seat (cat-owner.l4; "the owner of a cat", ss 4, 5, 6,
--     14, 18, 23, 25). Each answer is the baseline export's own answer, wrapped in this layer's answer types;
--   - the person getting a cat, by sale or gift: s 23 bars the transfer of a cat not microchipped or sterilised and
--     gives "the purchaser" the free sterilisation voucher (s 23(2)(b)). They ask whether the cat may be passed to them
--     as it is. The baseline's answer, worded for the transferor, is reworded for them;
--   - the veterinarian or microchip implanter: ss 15, 20 and 21 put on them the duties to notify the microchip database
--     company within 7 days and to give the owner a certificate of sterilisation, s 17 bars interfering with a
--     microchip, and ss 14(3), 18(3) say their certificate of exemption cannot apply to a cat under 6 months. These
--     rules are not in the baseline; they are encoded here, as helpers, from the deposited text.
-- The local government, the microchip database company and the approved cat breeder are not seats here: a local
-- government is never a seat, and the database company's duty (s 16) and breeding (s 35 onward) are outside the
-- baseline's scope. A breeder's s 18(2)(b) exemption is asked of the owner.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it is
-- FALSE, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, with the same name, type and
-- @desc. All are BOOLEAN; FALSE gives does not arise:
--   - for the owner: `my cat is registered with a local government` (the tag, s 6; when the registration ends and
--     renewing from 1 November, reg 12); `I am applying to register my cat, or to renew its registration` (whether it
--     must be refused, s 9; the fee, Sch 3); `I am giving away or selling my cat` (s 23); `my details as the cat's owner
--     have changed` (the 7 days to notify, s 25);
--   - for the veterinarian or implanter: `I have implanted a microchip in the cat` (s 15) and `I have sterilised the
--     cat` (ss 20, 21).
-- The person getting a cat is in the transfer by being in the role, so their question takes none. Questions that arise
-- for every owner (who is the owner, the 6-month day, the duties to register, microchip and sterilise, the number of
-- cats, the fines) and for every veterinarian or implanter (whether a certificate can apply, interfering with a
-- microchip, the fine) take none.
--
-- The owner's rules are in cat-owner.l4; this module calls them and restates none. Its own helpers reword the s 23
-- answer and encode ss 14(3), 15, 17, 18(3), 20 and 21 for the veterinarian or implanter. No exported question takes a
-- DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Cat Act 2011 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I own or keep a cat`
    `I am getting a cat from its owner, by sale or as a gift`
    `I am a veterinarian or a microchip implanter`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Date answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `on` HAS `the day` IS A DATE

-- s 20 needs a notice only for a microchipped cat.
DECLARE `Notice to the database` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no notice is needed: the cat is not microchipped (s 20)`

-- The baseline's own answer types, with `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `Registration duty, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Registration duty`

DECLARE `Microchip duty, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Microchip duty`

DECLARE `Sterilisation duty, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Sterilisation duty`

DECLARE `Registration outcome, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Registration outcome`

DECLARE `When registration ends, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `When registration ends`

DECLARE `Transfer answer, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Transfer answer`

DECLARE `How many cats, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `How many cats`

-- s 23 from the side of the person getting the cat.
DECLARE `May the cat be passed to me` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `yes: you are a body named in reg 9, so s 23 does not apply (reg 19)`
    `not unless it is microchipped first: the owner commits an offence otherwise (s 23(1))`
    `not unless it is sterilised first, or the owner gives you a free sterilisation voucher (s 23(2))`
    `yes (s 23)`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- Lists every value, with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Transfer answer`
GIVETH A `May the cat be passed to me`
`for the person getting the cat` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `yes: the transfer is to a body named in reg 9 (reg 19)` THEN `yes: you are a body named in reg 9, so s 23 does not apply (reg 19)`
    WHEN `not unless it is microchipped first (s 23(1))` THEN `not unless it is microchipped first: the owner commits an offence otherwise (s 23(1))`
    WHEN `not unless it is sterilised first, or I give the new owner a free sterilisation voucher (s 23(2))` THEN `not unless it is sterilised first, or the owner gives you a free sterilisation voucher (s 23(2))`
    WHEN `yes (s 23)` THEN `yes (s 23)`

-- s 15: "A microchip implanter who implants a microchip in a cat must, within 7 days after the microchip is implanted,
-- give notice in writing ... to the microchip database company for that cat." s 20: "A veterinarian who sterilises a
-- microchipped cat must, within 7 days after sterilising the cat, give notice in writing ... of the sterilisation of the
-- cat to the microchip database company for that cat." Counted as the baseline counts s 25: the day plus 7, by the day
-- serial, because jl4-service rejects a DATE PLUS a NUMBER (the stable CLI accepts it).
GIVEN `the day it was done` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`7 days after` `the day it was done` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day it was done` PLUS 7)

-- ss 14(3), 18(3): "A certificate referred to in subsection (2) [(2)(a)] cannot apply in respect of a cat that is under 6
-- months of age."
GIVEN `the cat's date of birth` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a certificate of exemption can apply to the cat` IF
    `my cat has reached 6 months of age` `the cat's date of birth` `the day`

-- s 17: "A person must not, without reasonable excuse, remove or interfere with a microchip implanted in a cat."
-- Penalty: a fine of $5 000. ss 15, 20, 21 each carry "Penalty: a fine of $5 000."
`the fine for a veterinarian's or implanter's offence` MEANS 5000

§§ `For the owner, or the person who keeps the cat`

§§§ `s 4 -- am I the owner, and the 6-month day`

@export Am I the owner of this cat (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `how I stand` IS A `How I stand to the cat` @desc How you are connected to the cat
      `my cat is registered with a local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cat is registered with a local government under s 9
      `there is evidence I do not keep it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a database record only: whether there is evidence that you do not in fact ordinarily keep and care for the cat
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I the owner of this cat under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN `yes if` (`Am I the owner of this cat` `how I stand` `my cat is registered with a local government` `there is evidence I do not keep it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export On what day does my cat reach 6 months of age (Cat Act 2011 (WA) ss 5, 14, 18)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your cat's date of birth, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`On what day does my cat reach 6 months of age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN `on` (`When does my cat reach 6 months of age` `my cat's date of birth`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 5, 6, 14, 18 -- registering, the tag, microchipping and sterilising`

@export Must I have my cat registered (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your cat's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
      `days I have kept the cat` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole days you have kept the cat
      `days I have lived in WA` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole days you have been resident in Western Australia
      `where my cat is` IS A `Where my cat is` @desc Where the cat is, or who has custody of it
      `weeks in SAFE foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc If in foster care placed by a SAFE entity: total weeks in foster care
      `my cat is now registered with that local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is now registered with the local government of the district where it is ordinarily kept
GIVETH A `Registration duty, if it arises`
`Must my cat be registered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN `the answer is` (`Must I have my cat registered` `my cat's date of birth` `the day` `days I have kept the cat` `days I have lived in WA` `where my cat is` `weeks in SAFE foster care` `my cat is now registered with that local government`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my cat be wearing its registration tag (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 6; Cat Regulations 2012 reg 10)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my cat is registered with a local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cat is registered with a local government under s 9
      `my cat is in a public place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is in a place to which the public has lawful access
      `my cat is being exhibited at a recognised cat show` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is being exhibited at a show held by one of the cat bodies named in reg 10(1), or an affiliate
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my cat wear its registration tag` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN
        IF NOT `my cat is registered with a local government`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must my cat be wearing its tag` `my cat is registered with a local government` `my cat is in a public place` `my cat is being exhibited at a recognised cat show`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I have my cat microchipped (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 14)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your cat's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
      `my cat is microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat has been implanted with a microchip by a microchip implanter
      `a vet has certified a microchip may harm my cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a veterinarian's certificate says implanting a microchip may adversely affect the cat's health and welfare
GIVETH A `Microchip duty, if it arises`
`Must my cat be microchipped` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN `the answer is` (`Must I have my cat microchipped` `my cat's date of birth` `the day` `my cat is microchipped` `a vet has certified a microchip may harm my cat`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I have my cat sterilised (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 18)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your cat's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
      `my cat is sterilised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat has been made permanently infertile by surgery by a veterinarian
      `a vet has certified sterilising may harm my cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a veterinarian's certificate says sterilising may adversely affect the cat's health and welfare
      `I am an approved breeder keeping it for breeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold an approval to breed cats under s 37 and own this cat for breeding
GIVETH A `Sterilisation duty, if it arises`
`Must my cat be sterilised` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN `the answer is` (`Must I have my cat sterilised` `my cat's date of birth` `the day` `my cat is sterilised` `a vet has certified sterilising may harm my cat` `I am an approved breeder keeping it for breeding`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 9, Sch 3, reg 12 -- applying, the fee, and how long registration lasts`

@export Must the local government refuse to register my cat (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am applying to register my cat, or to renew its registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying to a local government to register your cat, or to renew its registration (s 8, reg 12)
      `my cat's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your cat's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day the application is decided` IS A DATE @desc The day the application is decided, ISO 8601
      `I am under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, the applicant, are under 18
      `where my cat is` IS A `Where my cat is` @desc Where the cat is, or who has custody of it
      `weeks in SAFE foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc If in foster care placed by a SAFE entity: total weeks in foster care
      `my cat is microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat has been implanted with a microchip by a microchip implanter
      `a vet has certified a microchip may harm my cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a veterinarian's certificate says implanting a microchip may adversely affect the cat's health and welfare
      `my cat is sterilised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat has been made permanently infertile by surgery by a veterinarian
      `a vet has certified sterilising may harm my cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a veterinarian's certificate says sterilising may adversely affect the cat's health and welfare
      `I am an approved breeder keeping it for breeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold an approval to breed cats under s 37 and own this cat for breeding
      `my convictions in the last 3 years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many offences against the Cat Act, Dog Act 1976 or Animal Welfare Act 2002 you have been convicted of in the previous 3 years
GIVETH A `Registration outcome, if it arises`
`Must the local government refuse my application to register my cat` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN
        IF NOT `I am applying to register my cat, or to renew its registration`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`Must my registration be refused` `my cat's date of birth` `the day the application is decided` `I am under 18` `where my cat is` `weeks in SAFE foster care` `my cat is microchipped` `a vet has certified a microchip may harm my cat` `my cat is sterilised` `a vet has certified sterilising may harm my cat` `I am an approved breeder keeping it for breeding` `my convictions in the last 3 years`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most the registration fee for my cat can be, in dollars (Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 3)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am applying to register my cat, or to renew its registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying to a local government to register your cat, or to renew its registration (s 8, reg 12)
      `the term` IS A `Registration term` @desc Registration for one year, 3 years or the life of the cat (reg 12(1))
      `it is a renewal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are renewing an existing registration rather than applying for a first grant
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you make the application, ISO 8601
      `I am a pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an eligible pensioner under the Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most my cat's registration fee can be` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN
        IF NOT `I am applying to register my cat, or to renew its registration`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`What is the most my registration fee can be` `the term` `it is a renewal` `the day I apply` `I am a pensioner`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export When does my cat's registration end (Cat Regulations 2012 reg 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my cat is registered with a local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cat is registered with a local government under s 9
      `the term` IS A `Registration term` @desc Registration for one year, 3 years or the life of the cat (reg 12(1))
      `the day it takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The day the registration takes effect, from the registration certificate, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `When registration ends, if it arises`
`When will my cat's registration end` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN
        IF NOT `my cat is registered with a local government`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`When does my cat's registration end` `the term` `the day it takes effect`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can I renew my cat's registration today so that it takes effect from 1 November (Cat Regulations 2012 reg 12(2)(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my cat is registered with a local government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cat is registered with a local government under s 9
      `the day I would renew` IS A DATE @desc The day you would renew, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I renew my cat's registration today to take effect from 1 November` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN
        IF NOT `my cat is registered with a local government`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can I renew today to take effect from 1 November` `the day I would renew`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 23, 25 -- giving my cat away, and telling them of a change`

@export May I give away or sell my cat (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 23; Cat Regulations 2012 reg 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am giving away or selling my cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are selling your cat or giving it to someone else (a transfer, s 3)
      `to a body named in reg 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat goes to Cat Haven, the RSPCA WA, a SAFE entity, a cat management facility, veterinary premises or the Commonwealth biosecurity department
      `the cat is microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is microchipped
      `a vet's microchip certificate applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner is satisfied a veterinarian's certificate under s 14(2) applies to the cat
      `the cat is sterilised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is sterilised
      `a vet's sterilisation certificate applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner is satisfied a veterinarian's certificate under s 18(2)(a) applies to the cat
      `the new owner is an approved breeder buying it to breed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new owner is an approved cat breeder taking the cat for breeding
      `a free sterilisation voucher is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner gives the new owner a voucher to have the cat sterilised later by a veterinarian at no cost to them
GIVETH A `Transfer answer, if it arises`
`May I give away or sell my cat as it is` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN
        IF NOT `I am giving away or selling my cat`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`May I give away or sell my cat` `to a body named in reg 9` `the cat is microchipped` `a vet's microchip certificate applies` `the cat is sterilised` `a vet's sterilisation certificate applies` `the new owner is an approved breeder buying it to breed` `a free sterilisation voucher is given`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By what day must I tell the local government and the microchip database of a change to my details (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 25)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my details as the cat's owner have changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your name, address or other details recorded for the cat with the local government or the microchip database have changed (s 25)
      `the day of the change` IS A DATE @desc The day your details (for example your address) changed, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`By what day must I give notice of the change to my details` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN
        IF NOT `my details as the cat's owner have changed`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `by` (`By when must I give notice of the change` `the day of the change`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 79(3)(h), the fines`

@export How many cats may I keep at my home (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 79(3)(h); Cat (Uniform Local Provisions) Regulations 2013)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a local law limits cats at my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a local law of your local government limits the number of cats that may be kept at premises like yours
      `the local law's number` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of cats the local law allows at your premises
      `a cat organisation member lives here` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a current member of one of the cat organisations in Cat Regulations 2012 reg 23(c) is ordinarily resident at the premises
      `additional cats approved` IS A NUMBER @desc The additional number of cats your local government has approved for the premises, 0 if none
GIVETH A `How many cats, if it arises`
`How many cats may I keep at my home` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN `the answer is` (`How many cats may I keep here` `a local law limits cats at my home` `the local law's number` `a cat organisation member lives here` `additional cats approved`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most a court can fine me for this cat offence, in dollars (Cat Act 2011 (WA); Cat (Uniform Local Provisions) Regulations 2013)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most a court can fine me for this cat offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN amount (`What is the most I can be fined` `the offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I am given an infringement notice for this cat offence, how much is it, in dollars (Cat Regulations 2012 Sch 2; Cat (Uniform Local Provisions) Regulations 2013 reg 13)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much is an infringement notice for this cat offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I own or keep a cat` THEN amount (`How much is the infringement notice` `the offence`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the person getting a cat, by sale or as a gift`

§§§ `s 23 -- may the cat be passed to me as it is`

@export May the owner sell or give me the cat as it is (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 23; Cat Regulations 2012 reg 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `to a body named in reg 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat goes to Cat Haven, the RSPCA WA, a SAFE entity, a cat management facility, veterinary premises or the Commonwealth biosecurity department
      `the cat is microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is microchipped
      `a vet's microchip certificate applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner is satisfied a veterinarian's certificate under s 14(2) applies to the cat
      `the cat is sterilised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is sterilised
      `a vet's sterilisation certificate applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner is satisfied a veterinarian's certificate under s 18(2)(a) applies to the cat
      `the new owner is an approved breeder buying it to breed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new owner is an approved cat breeder taking the cat for breeding
      `a free sterilisation voucher is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner gives the new owner a voucher to have the cat sterilised later by a veterinarian at no cost to them
GIVETH A `May the cat be passed to me`
`May the owner sell or give me the cat as it is` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am getting a cat from its owner, by sale or as a gift` THEN `for the person getting the cat` (`May I give away or sell my cat` `to a body named in reg 9` `the cat is microchipped` `a vet's microchip certificate applies` `the cat is sterilised` `a vet's sterilisation certificate applies` `the new owner is an approved breeder buying it to breed` `a free sterilisation voucher is given`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the veterinarian or microchip implanter`

§§§ `ss 14(3), 15, 17, 18(3), 20, 21 -- certificates, microchips and sterilisation`

@export Can a certificate I give exempting this cat from microchipping or sterilisation apply to it (Cat Act 2011 (WA) ss 14(2), (3), 18(2)(a), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the cat's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The cat's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my certificate exempting this cat from microchipping or sterilisation apply to it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a veterinarian or a microchip implanter` THEN `yes if` (`a certificate of exemption can apply to the cat` `the cat's date of birth` `the day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By when must I tell the microchip database company about a microchip I implanted (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have implanted a microchip in the cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, as a microchip implanter, have implanted a microchip in the cat (s 15)
      `the day it was implanted` IS A DATE @desc The day you implanted the microchip, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Date answer`
`By when must I tell the database company about the microchip I implanted` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a veterinarian or a microchip implanter` THEN
        IF NOT `I have implanted a microchip in the cat`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `by` (`7 days after` `the day it was implanted`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By when must I tell the microchip database company that I sterilised the cat (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 20)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have sterilised the cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, as a veterinarian, have sterilised the cat (ss 20, 21)
      `the cat is microchipped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cat is microchipped
      `the day it was sterilised` IS A DATE @desc The day you sterilised the cat, ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Notice to the database`
`By when must I tell the database company that I sterilised the cat` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a veterinarian or a microchip implanter` THEN
        IF NOT `I have sterilised the cat`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE IF `the cat is microchipped` THEN `by` (`7 days after` `the day it was sterilised`) ELSE `no notice is needed: the cat is not microchipped (s 20)`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I give the owner a certificate of sterilisation (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 21)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have sterilised the cat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, as a veterinarian, have sterilised the cat (ss 20, 21)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I give the owner a certificate of sterilisation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a veterinarian or a microchip implanter` THEN
        IF NOT `I have sterilised the cat`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I remove or interfere with a microchip implanted in a cat (Cat Act 2011 (WA) s 17)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a reasonable excuse, such as a veterinary reason, for removing or interfering with the microchip
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I remove or interfere with a microchip in a cat` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a veterinarian or a microchip implanter` THEN `yes if` `I have a reasonable excuse`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for breaking one of these duties (Cat Act 2011 (WA) ss 15, 17, 20, 21)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for breaking a veterinarian's or implanter's duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a veterinarian or a microchip implanter` THEN amount `the fine for a veterinarian's or implanter's offence`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
